md=f'''# Batch15 independent component review\n\n**Result: bounded component evidence passes. The 77-row consumer index is proposed for lead promotion.** Four new designs, AST-CRW-001–004, extend the 73-design catalogue. Gathered curtain and open drawer exports are state derivatives; they add no designs, registered berths or people. The reviewer changed no authored component or canonical index.\n\n## Programme and craft\n\nThe reviewer read the actual D03 handoff and contract and inspected both supplied reference images. The photograph shows a stacked bunk, curtains, ladder/upper guard, personal shelves and local lights. This batch intentionally tests one editable single-place frame reused twice in a generous relative studio fixture. It does not establish a cabin polygon, recovered two-bed room, stack headroom or safe climbing. The 400-person crew includes the player and an existing colleague; host/berth-key reconciliation and colleague identity remain open.\n\nActual imported views show deliberately crowned padding, warm draped cloth, economical painted rails/feet, supported sage pleats, useful empty personal shelves/drawer and a compact mounted shield/shelf. These are practical staff fittings, materially distinct from passenger luxury and the clinical segmented deck. Frame dimensions are manually editable semantic geometry/source coordinates; the dimension summary is not a working resizing rig. Only the exported configuration is checked.\n\nAll 2,302 protected files and all 73 prior raw JSON and decoded object rows remain unchanged. Every old normalized record is preserved verbatim in the proposed 77-row index.\n\n## Source, native geometry and actual support\n\nAll{parts} semantic mesh parts connect through actual triangle contacts to a floor-supported part or the 004 mounting backplate. The latter is joined to the real 001 headboard with four physical opposing source/native surface witnesses. This is geometric support, not attachment strength or load certification. All{physical} physical markers lie on their named actual source/native surfaces with witnessed outward normals. The two nonphysical placement/aim markers remain explicitly separate.\n\nActual native hierarchy, evaluated geometry, material/texture bytes and per-material position, split-normal and UV corner attributes pass. Runtime evaluated copies consolidate by material and moving ownership while retaining semantic source parts. Costs below are actual file counts, not engine measurements.\n\n| Design | Source parts | Closed triangles | Native mesh nodes | Collision shapes | Sampled max inflation |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n{table}\n\n## Motion and useful spaces\n\n{void_count} distinct declared useful boxes pass complete inset triangle/box and collision feasibility checks, with empty and solid-control probes. The drawer’s complete 0.24m stroke includes every wall, runner, pull and physical moving marker. Continuous triangle SAT begins at t=0 and distinguishes proper constant-plane runner bearing contact from penetration. Both endpoints and the complete swept useful boxes remain clear; runner overlap stays at least 0.155m. Native open geometry and ownership match the authored transformation.\n\nThe curtain’s real source parameter combines affine span/leading motion with nonlinear pleat depth preserving developed segment length. Analytical full bounds and{posecount} independently captured actual source poses retain ring support, grip ownership and fixed-part clearance. Closed/gathered native geometry agrees. The report distinguishes these geometric tests from physical cloth simulation. Fifty-two ordinary seated/standing side rays plus eight deliberately clear top/bottom/end rays bound the privacy claim. Open ends, top and under-hem space remain unprotected.\n\nThe independent paired check transforms actual native geometry/proposals in closed, open, mixed-privacy and all-open states. Conservative full motion bounds preserve the central 1.4m strip and both foot approaches. Mounted shelf-to-pillow separation is 78mm and the module stays outside the declared central rest-use prism. Eight displayed instances remain four designs and zero registered berths. These clearances are proposals, not bodies, carts or a certified room.\n\n## Finish and collision\n\nCorrected before acceptance: a floating blanket, a faceted track-normal mismatch, shelf gussets entering retrieval space, headboard-support exposed coincident faces, and 50 tiny ring/tape face coincidences. Final advisory axial screen has zero exposed same-facing candidates; it is supplemented by actual imported pixel inspection, not claimed as universal visibility analysis. Initial and superseded evidence is retained.\n\nCollision profiles preserve actual under-frame, support-slat, shelf/drawer, grip and approach spaces. The rail lips have separate thin structural profiles. The blanket is deliberately visual textile without independent collision: a convex-distance vertex bound proves its complete planar surface is within 80mm of the mattress hull; the full compound is no farther away. Flexible curtain panel prisms have an explicit 3mm profile bound; sampled closed/gathered undercoverage is 0.728/1.484mm. Fine rings, tapes, grip and assembly fasteners remain disclosed actor-collision omissions. The track capsule has a separately disclosed conservative review approximation. The nominally exact pillow hull has a measured 7.314 micrometre deviation, accepted within the explicit 20 micrometre geometric comparison tolerance used for support contacts. Sampled inflation is not a continuous global distance maximum or runtime physics acceptance.\n\n## Rebuilds and actual images\n\nReviewer-controlled clean stages start with{reb_inputs['crew_rest']} rest inputs and{reb_inputs['crew_personal']} personal inputs, with no pre-existing new outputs or QA input. All six GLBs reproduce byte-for-byte. Editable mesh/UV, hierarchy, drivers, shape keys, modifiers/properties and used-material/evaluated signatures match. Every generated JSON matches after normalizing only source .blend binary hashes. Python open events plus native-loaded image witnesses bind the closure; this is not an OS-syscall-complete trace. Original cloth pixels also reproduce from their deterministic drawing source.\n\n{image_count} final imported-GLB pictures were independently inspected and hash-bound: four corrected rest/privacy views, two unchanged storage views and four current paired/mounted views. Earlier mounted/context captures and the lead’s first rejected hash-guard run remain historical. Physical join corrections received actual affected recaptures. Later allowance-only metadata changes were checked separately against unchanged exact geometry and reproduced before final capture.\n\n## Remaining adoption gates\n\nNo original engine integration, cabin/room or berth-key adoption, structural loads, runtime performance, live sleeping/curtain/drawer/inventory controls, actual electrical lighting/photometry, acoustic privacy, six-species/body/hand reach or accessibility certification is claimed. Dry padding does not supply aquatic Baelin housing or Mantelid cocoons; no Mindo service ports, charging needs, roommate story or new crew allocation is invented.\n'''
